ubstring of the row text>\", \"count\": n}, ...]}  (default: none = [])\n21\tLast stdout line: `ERRORLIST-VERDICT: OK|MISMATCH|FAIL <json path>`.\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\timport argparse, glob, hashlib, json, os, re, shutil, sys, time\n24\t\n25\tHERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))\n26\tROOT = os.path.dirname(HERE)\n27\tsys.path.insert(0, HERE)\n28\tsys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\"))\n29\t# LAZY LabVIEW IMPORTS (card 81-1, 2026-09-25): the offline re-verdict (`find_reusable` / `reverdict`, used by\n30\t# cycle_runner.errorlist_hook when the bed md5 is unchanged) must import nothing LabVIEW-side, so gscript /\n31\t# lv_errorlist / bench_prep are bound only by `_lv_imports()`, which main() calls first. Same modules, same order.\n32\tg = E = labview_handles = None\n33\tCLAUDEDEV = r\"C:\\Program Files\\National Instruments\\LabVIEW 2026\\user.lib\\claudeDev\"   # == gscript.CLAUDEDEV\n34\t\n35\tEVID = \"user 2026-09-24 error-list check at cycle start\"\n36\t\n37\t\n38\tdef _lv_imports():\n39\t    global g, E, labview_handles\n40\t    if g is None:\n41\t        import gscript as _g\n42\t        import lv_errorlist as _E\n43\t        from bench_prep import labview_handles as _lh\n44\t        g, E, labview_handles = _g, _E, _lh\n45\t        E.EVIDENCE = EVID\n46\t\n47\t\n48\tBENCH = os.path.join(HERE, \"bench\")\n49\t# 2026-09-24 card chat-C2: external search (WebSearch, \"LabVIEW scripting read selected objects block diagram\n50\t# Selection List\") found no route other than a VI Server property node on TopLevelDiagram.Selection List[]; the\n51\t# ActiveX VirtualInstrument interface has no diagram access (toolkit-capabilities.md:666), and building an op VI is\n52\t# outside a labview=read card. So the uid is not read here; the after-capture of the diagram is the record.\n53\tUID_ROUTE = \"none: needs a Selection List[] 6349400 op (unbuilt; card labview=read) - screenshot recorded\"\n54\tCOUNT_RE = re.compile(r\"(\\d+)\\s*errors?\\s*and\\s*warnings?\",